  "question": "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & x \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $|A|=5$, find $x$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Expand along $R_1$.<br />$|A| = 1 \\times \\begin{vmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} - 0 \\times (...) + x \\times \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\end{vmatrix}$<br />Evaluating:<br />$1 \\times (2 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot 1) = 2$<br />$x \\times (0 \\cdot 0 - 3 \\cdot 2) = x \\times (-6) = -6x$<br />So,<br />$2 - 6x = 5$<br />$-6x = 3$<br />$x = -\\frac{1}{2}$",
